Description: Raytro, 4k intro for GNU/Linux by glaze/wAMMA, released in 2008
 First 4k intro of glaze (Timo Wirén) of the group wAMMA, released
 at Pouet.net in February 2008: a real-time ray tracer that renders
 a sphereflake with Amiga-style textures, a room with reflective
 cylinders and the wAMMA logo, with moving lights, reflections and
 shadows. There is no music: the whole 4 KB were spent on graphics code.
 .
 Press F to toggle fullscreen and any other key to quit. Run with
 --fullscreen to start in fullscreen, as the original release did.
